        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Yes, absolutely. With many new construction homes in Van Alstyne featuring slab foundations, our garage floor shelters are an excellent option. We coordinate with builders to integrate the shelter seamlessly into your garage floor during construction or can install it in an existing slab.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Are there any rebates or financial assistance programs for storm shelters in Van Alstyne, TX?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">While specific local rebates can vary, Van Alstyne residents may be eligible for federal or state programs, or even local grants. We can provide guidance on potential rebate opportunities and help you navigate the information available to make your storm shelter more affordable.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How long does a typical storm shelter installation take in Van Alstyne?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">The installation time for a storm shelter in Van Alstyne can vary based on the shelter type and site specifics. Most residential installations, such as garage floor or above-ground safe rooms, can be completed within a day or two. We'll provide a clear timeline with your free written estimate.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">What kind of maintenance do storm shelters in Van Alstyne require?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Generally, storm shelters require minimal maintenance. We recommend regular checks to ensure the door mechanism functions smoothly, ventilation is clear, and the interior is kept clean and free of debris. For underground shelters, checking for moisture buildup periodically is also a good practice.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
